24/06/99

   o ZMailer - If Use Call List is enabled in the preferences, the ZMailer
       will also add mail calls to the global 'number of calls received'
       counters: the "all time", "today" and "this hour" ones used to
       generate statistics and graphs around the BBS.
          Why does it make sense for this to happen? If Use Call List is
       enabled, the lower graph on the ANSI Watcher ("Session:") will
       match the upper one; The upper one is generated from the global
       'all time' statistics, while the lower one takes it's data from
       the LastCalls list (the one which is displayed in the watcher).
       Before, Use Call List ment that ZMailer added to the LastCalls
       list but not the global calls list, hence the Global calls list
       was out of sync with the LastCalls.  If you receive a lot of
       mailer calls, you'll have noticed this in the graphs and that
       the Calls Todays counter missed mailer calls.
   o FileControl - No file related CC commands would work without a user
       online.  Fixed.
   o FileControl - Changed CC expansion code to be a bit more efficient.
   o FileControl - Only those CC commands that relate to users are skipped
       if no user is online.
   o FileControl - When outputting a file size in MegaBytes using the CC
       and not specifying the MEGA argument (i.e. dynamic use of byte, KB,
       MB), FileControl was displaying a number of around 1x10^300. Fixed.
   o ZMailer - Fixed serial line restrictions.  Things like "No Answer"
       (between xx and xx hours) and "Mail Only" should work now. (Alex,
       mate, you said this worked in ZeusNet, yet I see a "break" not a
       "return( la )" here! ;)
   o Connector - This was, like, man, totally missing any line access
       restriction code... So in it goes, and now Connector can be
       told to not answer the phone between whatever times you want.
   o ZMailer - Major overhaul to the OwnDevUnit code. You should now not
       see any crashes when another program (e.g. Miami) takes over
       the serial line from ZMailer. Also, when ZMailer is "Attempting
       to lock device" you will be able to quit, (de)iconify and even
       queue outbound calls - although there could be a 5 second reaction
       delay in visible changes due to OwnDevUnit (but it's better than
       waiting until the other program finishes, I think).

