03/07/99

   o ZMailer - Any crashes related to Miami and OwnDevUnit (i.e. in Miami
       click Dial, Cancel, Dial and watch ZMailer crash) should be fixed.
       Miami appears to have a buggy OwnDevUnit implementation, where it
       will tell programs that the device is free for use, but will go and
       allocate it anyway. ZMailer will try to work its way out of the mess
       by freeing OwnDevUnit and waiting again, but if it does not succeed
       it exit gracefully.
   o ZMailer - When in a "No Answer" period, ZMailer will log any incoming
       RING's. This is really just a personal addition which I wanted, so
       it should eventually be switchable. Eventually I'll get around to
       writing some better CallerID code -- then you'll be able to keep a
       log of calls to non-BBS lines if you have a spare caller ID capable
       modem and serial port!
   o ZAPP - Changed XPK calls/identifiers for the new includes.
   o ZAPP - It looks like it is actually usable now!  I've spent some time
       working through it, and I've managed to get it working quickly -
       all that jerky ANSI you got before is GONE!  Originally this new
       code had a side effect of stopping long ZAPP transfers early
       (playing a CD audio track for example), but this has also been
       fixed.  Some final clean ups, new docs, and it's ready to roll with
       Zeus 1.2.
   o FakeXfer - Will now copy files to the TempUpload dir if they are not
       already there, making it easier now to maintain your BBS using just
       the ANSI interface.
   o ZAPP Prefs - Added "Download Directory" string gadget, which sets the
       DIRECTORY field of env:ZAPP/XFER.prefs.

